= Round70: P-192 point-action qualification
Local exact Rust checks; scientific standing unverified.
#image("outcomes.svg", width: 100%)
The native P-192 record retains two special fibers, four elliptic quotient models, seven rational and six marked streams. All 24 based order tests have nonzero images and nonzero order-r multiples. Each sign-adjusted scalar prefix fails at its second point. Polynomial identities, model membership and source group controls pass.

The small-field attempt stopped at an assertion requiring wrong-Z rejection in every fiber. The frozen control required a rejection among retained points. No complete small-field panel is claimed and no scientific retry was made.

Source was published before data. A compile type fix was separately published before data. Fresh P-192 output matches byte for byte; changing an order boolean is rejected. The full derivations, limitations, commands and primary-source links are in report.md. The exact run record and stderr remain alongside this report.

The canonical elliptic pullback/pushforward cancels by a principal conjugate-pair divisor. The boundary torus has order p squared plus p plus one, coprime to all five supplied P-192-run orders. Neither calculation supplies the missing noncanonical scalar action.

Next: a costed horizontal principal relation with an explicit action, followed by an implementable orbit representative; or explicit transport between changing family parameters. Independent signed scientific review remains pending.
